Subject: [PATCH 05704/11362] [outer-loop] find + document: human replay corpus
 has 144 winning trajectories, staging bug hides them

Operator asked: "don't we have the human generated game event solutions
handy to help with the complete TRM training?" -- a direct challenge to
verify what data actually exists before assuming the 69-Carnot-agent-level
corpus was the only option in yesterday's TRM-as-generator note.

Investigated data/arc_public_demo_human_replay_corpus/ directly (raw
parquet + staged shards, not just the capability spec's prose):

FOUND: the raw HuggingFace mirror (CC BY 4.0, staged by exp4495 on
2026-06-20) has 340 human play sessions across all 25 public ARC-AGI-3
games, 144 of them complete wins reaching levels 6-10, ~90,000+ actions
total. Verified per-step richness directly: each trajectory step carries
frame, action taken, state (NOT_FINISHED/GAME_OVER/WIN), a running
levels_completed counter, and available_actions. Cross-validated the
segmentation is real, not just self-reported: for one sk48 session,
actions_by_level claims level 1 completes at action index 37; the raw
per-step trajectory confirms levels_completed flips from 0 to 1 exactly
at step 37.

FOUND A REAL BUG: the *staged* shards actually wired for training (14,797
rows, carnot.arc_human_replay.frame_action_delta.v1) have level_progress=
0.0 in literally every row, including a full 1564-step winning wa30
session start to finish. exp4495's schema conversion dropped won/
levels_completed/win_levels/state/available_actions entirely when
building the training shards -- the same class of corpus-artifact bug
this project has hit before (the n_win_states=0 trap). This also explains
why exp4490 (the original frame-change-predictor consumer) has sat
blocked_human_replay_corpus_not_cached since 2026-06-20 04:40 -- it ran
~1.5h before staging completed at 06:06 the same day, and appears never
retried in the two weeks since.

FOUND A REAL NUANCE: sessions include GAME_OVER/retry cycles mid-session
(confirmed across lp85/tu93/wa30), so a re-staging or training pipeline
needs to resolve the session-level `resets` markers before treating a
session as one continuous sequence.

Documented in docs/research-notes/human-replay-corpus-staging-bug-and-
opportunity-2026-07-04.md (full writeup, per-game win-count table, the
validation methodology, the open discrepancy in wa30's raw-vs-staged row
count). Updated docs/research-notes/trm-arc-action-sequence-generator-
2026-07-04.md's training-data-sufficiency open question (now resolved far
more favorably, superseding the 69-level corpus in priority). Updated
ops/verifier_gaps.md's GAP-ARC-TRM-TRAINED-ON-ARC entry in place (third
update on this gap, avoiding a fourth tracking location). Flagged in
ops/known-issues.md for planner pickup: the concrete next step is a narrow
re-staging fix (preserve win-segmentation fields, resolve reset
discontinuities) before either retrying exp4490 or building a TRM pilot.

